# Video. Clips are cheap to regenerate and expensive to store: `record.py --filmstrip`
# writes a PNG contact sheet alongside every clip, and the still strip is the artefact
# worth keeping -- it can be read in a note or a review, an mp4 cannot. Cite the
# filmstrip and the command that made the clip, not the clip.
#
# NOTE 10 mp4s were committed before this rule and stay tracked; gitignore does not
# untrack. Leave them: `l4_rope2_video/crossing_1_ep236_neither.mp4` is the only
# recorded evidence of a policy crossing rope 2 from reset.
*.mp4

# Agent scratch. Short-lived command output and intermediate artefacts live here so they
# never land in a project directory (a previous session buried 41 real documents under
# ~550 strays). Anything worth keeping is promoted to experiments/<id>/evidence/.
.kiro/tmp/
